title: '[pallet-revive] fix double deposit charge to parent contractinfo'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A contract that writes storage, calls back into itself, directly or through another contract,
    and then writes storage again now has each write counted once in its `ContractInfo`. Before,
    the writes made before the reentrant call were applied to the stored `ContractInfo` a second
    time when the outer call finished. This inflated `storage_items`, `storage_bytes`,
    `storage_item_deposit` and `storage_byte_deposit`, and the inflated values were kept across
    transactions: `ContractInfo` reported more storage items, bytes and deposit than the contract
    actually stored and held.

    Calls that do not reenter the same contract are not affected.

    No migration, configuration or integration change is needed. Existing `ContractInfo`
    entries are not rewritten: counters that were already inflated keep their values.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
